[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: workflow.STATE_TRACKING
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[STATE_TRACKING]
overview: Hybrid state tracking for multi-phase workflow tasks — TodoWrite for phase progress, a workplan file for plan/approvals/decisions
purpose: Survive context compaction, session restart, and long-running tasks. The agent must be able to resume work without losing the approved plan or the list of what's done.
principle: Ephemeral state (which step is next) goes in TodoWrite. Durable state (the plan, user approvals, deviations, out-of-scope notes) goes on disk.

[WHY_BOTH]
TodoWrite alone:
  - Good: built-in, visible to user, lightweight
  - Bad: doesn't survive session restart, doesn't hold structured plan content, can't capture approval history
Workplan file alone:
  - Good: durable, human-readable, captures everything
  - Bad: not shown in the live todo UI, easier to forget to update
Hybrid:
  - TodoWrite tracks phase-level progress (6 todos per task, one per phase)
  - Workplan file holds the plan, approvals, deviations, and final report
  - Both updated together; they stay consistent

[WORKPLAN_LOCATION]
path_active:   .claude/workplan/<slug>.md
path_archive:  .claude/workplan/archive/<ISO_DATE>-<slug>.md
slug_format:   lowercase, hyphen-separated, ≤40 chars, derived from user's request
               examples: "add-webhook-retries", "refactor-auth-middleware", "fix-login-race"

Multiple active workplans may coexist if the user juggles tasks. One workplan per task.

[WORKPLAN_LIFECYCLE]
1. CREATED at end of DISCOVER phase (Phase 1)
2. UPDATED after each phase transition and after each user response at a gate
3. ARCHIVED at end of REPORT phase (Phase 6): moved to archive/ with today's ISO date prefix
4. DELETED only if user explicitly says "drop the workplan" — default is to archive

Before starting any new turn on a workflow task, the agent MUST:
  - Check .claude/workplan/ for active workplans matching the current request
  - If found → load state, resume from the recorded phase, do NOT restart from Phase 1
  - If not found → start a new workplan at the end of DISCOVER

[WORKPLAN_TEMPLATE]
# Workplan: <user's request in one line>

**Slug:** <slug>
**Task type:** <feature | refactor | bugfix | other>
**Started:** <ISO datetime>
**Current phase:** <DISCOVER | PLAN | CONFIRM | IMPLEMENT | VERIFY | REPORT | ARCHIVED>
**Status:** <in-progress | awaiting-approval | blocked | done>

## Task
<Restated task. Confirm with user if restatement was needed.>

## Discovery
- **Similar patterns found:** <list or "none">
- **Relevant files:** <list with one-line purpose each>
- **Constraints from CLAUDE.md / CONSTRAINTS.toon:** <list>
- **Unknowns resolved in discovery:** <list>

## Plan
### Goal
<one sentence>

### Approach
<2-5 sentences: what and why>

### Files to change
- `<path>` — <what changes>

### Files to add
- `<path>` — <purpose>

### Files to delete
- `<path>` — <reason>

### Tests / verification
<how this will be proven>

### Risks / unknowns
<what could go wrong>

### Out of scope
<what was deliberately excluded>

### Rollback (refactor only)
<how to undo if needed>

## Gate log
- **<ISO datetime>** — Presented plan. User response: `<verbatim or paraphrased>`. Outcome: `<approved | amended | rejected>`.
- **<ISO datetime>** — <next gate event>

## Deviations
(Filled during IMPLEMENT phase if reality diverges from plan. Each entry forces a trip back to PLAN and CONFIRM.)
- **<ISO datetime>** — Discovered: `<what>`. Re-planned: `<how>`. User response: `<outcome>`.

## Verification
- [ ] <verification item from plan> — <result>
- [ ] <...>

## Report
<Final summary. Filled in Phase 6.>

## Unresolved
<Follow-ups, spawned tasks, anything the user should know.>

[TODOWRITE_USAGE]
At the start of a workflow task, the agent creates SIX todos, one per phase:
  1. [DISCOVER] <one-line task description>
  2. [PLAN] Design approach and write plan
  3. [CONFIRM] Present plan, wait for approval
  4. [IMPLEMENT] Execute approved plan
  5. [VERIFY] Prove change works
  6. [REPORT] Summarize for user

Each todo transitions: pending → in_progress (when phase starts) → completed (when phase exit criteria met).
Only ONE todo is in_progress at a time.
If a gate rejects the plan → the CONFIRM todo stays in_progress; the PLAN todo reopens.
If IMPLEMENT deviates → IMPLEMENT stays in_progress; a new "re-plan" sub-todo is added.

[CONSISTENCY_RULES]
- Workplan `Current phase` field MUST match the single in_progress TodoWrite entry
- Every user response at a gate MUST be appended to the "Gate log" section of the workplan BEFORE the agent does anything else
- Never update TodoWrite without also updating the workplan (and vice-versa)

[RESUMPTION_AFTER_COMPACTION_OR_RESTART]
If context was compacted or the session was restarted:
  1. First action: list .claude/workplan/*.md (not archive/)
  2. If any are in-progress, ask the user: "I see an active workplan for `<slug>`. Resume, or start fresh?"
  3. On resume: read the workplan file fully, restore TodoWrite state to match `Current phase`, continue
  4. On fresh start: offer to archive the stale workplan before beginning

[GITIGNORE_AND_CLAUDESIGNORE]
Workplans are local session state, not project history:
  - Add `.claude/workplan/` to the project's `.gitignore` (do not commit workplans)
  - Add `.claude/workplan/archive/` to the project's `.claudesignore` (don't load archives into context by default)
  - The active `.claude/workplan/*.md` files ARE loaded into context when the agent needs them
  - SETUP_PROMPT ensures both entries are present at init time

[WHEN_TO_SKIP_STATE_TRACKING]
If ESCAPE_HATCH applies (see ESCAPE_HATCH.toon) → no workplan is needed.
A trivial edit does not justify a workplan file. Skip TodoWrite for trivial tasks as well.

If unsure whether the task is trivial enough → create the workplan. Cost is one file write; benefit is resumability.
